{"title":"HIERARCHICAL REPRESENTATION OF OPTICALLY SCANNED DOCUMENTS","url":"https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cseconfwork/292/","authors":["George Nagy","Sharad C. Seth"],"year":1984,"venue":"Proceedings of the Seventh International Conference on Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Presents a hierarchical representation for optically scanned documents that preserves spatial organization and relationships among document components such as text, figures, subtitles, and captions. The representation supports recovery of logical relations including reading order."}
{"title":"Table structure recognition based on textblock arrangement and ruled line position","authors":["K. Itonori"],"year":1993,"abstract":"Early work on recognizing table structure from the arrangement of text blocks and ruled lines, addressing reconstruction of cell and table organization rather than table detection alone."}
{"title":"Recent Advances in the CLiDE Project: Logical Layout Analysis of Chemical Documents","url":"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/ci9601022","doi":"10.1021/ci9601022","authors":["Anikó Simon","A. Peter Johnson"],"year":1997,"published":"1997-01-27","venue":"Journal of Chemical Information and Computer Sciences","abstract":"Describes physical and logical layout analysis for chemical documents. Recognized page primitives are assigned logical roles using document-style knowledge, providing evidence for preserving semantic document structure above raw OCR and region detection."}
{"title":"A machine-learning approach for analyzing document layout structures with two reading orders","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0031320308000976","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2008.03.014","authors":["Chung-Chih Wu","Chien-Hsing Chou","Fu Chang"],"year":2008,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Studies document layout analysis where page elements may participate in different reading-order interpretations. It uses learned structural relationships rather than treating page segmentation as an unordered collection of boxes."}
{"title":"The Significance of Reading Order in Document Recognition and Its Evaluation","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICDAR.2013.141","doi":"10.1109/ICDAR.2013.141","authors":["Christian Clausner","Stefan Pletschacher","Apostolos Antonacopoulos"],"year":2013,"venue":"International Conference on Document Analysis and Recognition","abstract":"Examines reading order as a component of document recognition and discusses its representation and evaluation. It is directly relevant to preserving logical structure when converting document pages into machine-readable representations."}
{"title":"Reading order detection in visually-rich documents with multi-modal layout-aware relation prediction","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0031320324000657","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2024.110314","authors":["Liang Qiao","Can Li","Zhanzhan Cheng","Yunlu Xu","Yi Niu","Xi Li"],"year":2024,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Models reading order in visually rich documents through multimodal, layout-aware prediction of relations between page elements. The task goes beyond region detection by explicitly recovering structural ordering."}
{"title":"Detect-order-construct: A tree construction based approach for hierarchical document structure analysis","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0031320324005879","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2024.110836","authors":["Jiawei Wang","Kai Hu","Zhuoyao Zhong","Lei Sun","Qiang Huo"],"year":2024,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Addresses hierarchical document structure by detecting page objects, inferring reading order and structural relations, and constructing a document tree. It provides a representation that preserves both physical and logical organization."}
{"title":"Reading order detection on handwritten documents","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00521-022-06948-5","doi":"10.1007/s00521-022-06948-5","authors":["Lorenzo Quirós","Enrique Vidal"],"year":2022,"published":"2022-02-03","venue":"Neural Computing and Applications","abstract":"Studies reading-order recovery in handwritten documents using document structure and contextual relationships. Although the domain is handwritten material rather than workplace email, the structural ordering problem is transferable to preserving document semantics."}
{"title":"LayoutLM: Pre-training of Text and Layout for Document Image Understanding","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.13318","arxiv_id":"1912.13318","authors":["Yiheng Xu","Minghao Li","Lei Cui","Shaohan Huang","Furu Wei","Ming Zhou"],"year":2020,"venue":"KDD","abstract":"Introduces pretraining that jointly represents document text and two-dimensional layout information. The model demonstrates that spatial coordinates materially improve understanding of visually rich documents compared with text-only processing."}
{"title":"LayoutLMv2: Multi-modal Pre-training for Visually-Rich Document Understanding","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.14740","arxiv_id":"2012.14740","authors":["Yang Xu","Yiheng Xu","Tengchao Lv","Lei Cui","Furu Wei","Guoxin Wang","Yijuan Lu","Dinei Florencio","Cha Zhang","Wanxiang Che","Min Zhang","Lidong Zhou"],"year":2021,"venue":"ACL","abstract":"Extends document pretraining to jointly use text, layout, and visual image features. Its multimodal objectives explicitly encourage alignment between textual tokens and corresponding visual regions."}
{"title":"LayoutLMv3: Pre-training for Document AI with Unified Text and Image Masking","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.08387","arxiv_id":"2204.08387","doi":"10.1145/3503161.3548112","authors":["Yupan Huang","Tengchao Lv","Lei Cui","Yutong Lu","Furu Wei"],"year":2022,"venue":"ACM Multimedia","abstract":"Uses unified masking objectives across document text and page images while retaining layout information. It supports document tasks requiring joint access to textual, visual, and spatial evidence."}
{"title":"DocFormer: End-to-End Transformer for Document Understanding","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.11539","arxiv_id":"2106.11539","authors":["Srikar Appalaraju","Bhavan Jasani","Bhargava Urala Kota","Yusheng Xie","R. Manmatha"],"year":2021,"venue":"ICCV","abstract":"Presents an end-to-end multimodal transformer that combines text, visual appearance, and spatial information for document understanding. It is relevant to preserving page structure and associations between OCR content and visual regions."}
{"title":"OCR-free Document Understanding Transformer","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.15664","arxiv_id":"2111.15664","authors":["Geewook Kim","Teakgyu Hong","Moonbin Yim","Jeongyeon Nam","Jinyoung Park","Jinyeong Yim","Wonseok Hwang","Sangdoo Yun","Dongyoon Han","Seunghyun Park"],"year":2022,"venue":"ECCV","abstract":"Introduces Donut, an OCR-free document understanding model that maps document images directly to structured textual outputs. It demonstrates an alternative to OCR pipelines but does not by itself guarantee source-region provenance for every generated value."}
{"title":"StrucTexT: Structured Text Understanding with Multi-Modal Transformers","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.02923","arxiv_id":"2108.02923","authors":["Yulin Li","Yuxi Qian","Yuchen Yu","Xiameng Qin","Chengquan Zhang","Yan Liu","Kun Yao","Junyu Han","Jingtuo Liu","Errui Ding"],"year":2021,"abstract":"Uses multimodal transformers to model text segments together with visual and spatial information. It targets structured text understanding including entity labeling and linking, making explicit relations among document elements rather than treating text as a flat sequence."}
{"title":"BROS: A Pre-trained Language Model Focusing on Text and Layout for Better Key Information Extraction from Documents","url":"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/21322","doi":"10.1609/aaai.v36i10.21322","authors":["Teakgyu Hong","DongHyun Kim","Mingi Ji","Wonseok Hwang","Daehyun Nam","Sungrae Park"],"year":2022,"venue":"AAAI","abstract":"Pretrains representations of text together with two-dimensional layout for key-information extraction. Its relevance is primarily to spatially structured extraction; fixed-schema extraction results should not be interpreted as proof of arbitrary document or attachment understanding."}
{"title":"Doc2Graph: a Task Agnostic Document Understanding Framework based on Graph Neural Networks","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.11168","arxiv_id":"2208.11168","authors":["Andrea Gemelli","Sanket Biswas","Enrico Civitelli","Josep Lladós","Simone Marinai"],"year":2022,"abstract":"Represents document entities and their relationships as a graph and applies graph neural networks to document-understanding tasks. The graph formulation is relevant to preserving relations among regions rather than flattening document contents."}
{"title":"Unifying Vision, Text, and Layout for Universal Document Processing","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.02623","arxiv_id":"2212.02623","authors":["Zineng Tang","Ziyi Yang","Guoxin Wang","Yuwei Fang","Yang Liu","Chenguang Zhu","Michael Zeng","Cha Zhang","Mohit Bansal"],"year":2023,"venue":"CVPR","abstract":"Introduces a unified document model that jointly processes visual, textual, and layout information and can generate structured outputs for multiple document tasks. It provides evidence for sharing a multimodal representation across extraction and question-answering tasks."}
{"title":"DocLLM: A layout-aware generative language model for multimodal document understanding","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.00908","arxiv_id":"2401.00908","authors":["Dongsheng Wang","Natraj Raman","Mathieu Sibue","Zhiqiang Ma","Petr Babkin","Simerjot Kaur","Yulong Pei","Armineh Nourbakhsh","Xiaomo Liu"],"year":2024,"venue":"ACL","abstract":"Adds layout awareness to a generative language model for document understanding without requiring a conventional vision encoder. It targets forms, tables, and visually structured documents and is relevant to preserving spatial relationships during generative reasoning."}
{"title":"Pix2Struct: Screenshot Parsing as Pretraining for Visual Language Understanding","url":"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/lee23g.html","authors":["Kenton Lee","Mandar Joshi","Iulia Raluca Turc","Hexiang Hu","Fangyu Liu","Julian Martin Eisenschlos","Urvashi Khandelwal","Peter Shaw","Ming-Wei Chang","Kristina Toutanova"],"year":2023,"venue":"ICML","abstract":"Pretrains a vision-language model by learning to parse screenshots into simplified HTML-like structures. The approach is transferable to document and attachment understanding because it reconstructs structured visual content rather than optimizing only navigation or clicking."}
{"title":"LayoutMask: Enhance Text-Layout Interaction in Multi-modal Pre-training for Document Understanding","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.847/","authors":["Yi Tu","Ya Guo","Huan Chen","Jinyang Tang"],"year":2023,"venue":"ACL","abstract":"Improves multimodal document pretraining by strengthening interactions between textual tokens and their spatial layout. It is relevant to preserving text-region associations needed for structured extraction and evidence localization."}
{"title":"DocVQA: A Dataset for VQA on Document Images","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/WACV2021/html/Mathew_DocVQA_A_Dataset_for_VQA_on_Document_Images_WACV_2021_paper.html","authors":["Minesh Mathew","Dimosthenis Karatzas","C. V. Jawahar"],"year":2021,"venue":"WACV","abstract":"Introduces a large benchmark for answering natural-language questions from document images. The task requires understanding text together with document layout and visual structure, although standard answer evaluation is generally less precise than explicit bounding-box evidence grounding."}
{"title":"Document Visual Question Answering Challenge 2020","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.08899","arxiv_id":"2008.08899","authors":["Minesh Mathew","Ruben Tito","Dimosthenis Karatzas","R. Manmatha","C. V. Jawahar"],"year":2020,"abstract":"Reports the 2020 DocVQA challenge and its document-image question-answering tasks. It provides benchmark evidence for reasoning over visually structured documents but should not be interpreted as explicit source-region grounding unless a task supplies such supervision."}
{"title":"InfographicVQA","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.12756","arxiv_id":"2104.12756","authors":["Minesh Mathew","Viraj Bagal","Rubèn Pérez Tito","Dimosthenis Karatzas","Ernest Valveny","C. V. Jawahar"],"year":2022,"venue":"WACV","abstract":"Introduces question answering over infographics where information is distributed among text, graphics, and spatial layout. The benchmark is directly relevant to multimodal page understanding and transferable to image-rich workplace attachments."}
{"title":"Hierarchical multimodal transformers for Multi-Page DocVQA","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.05935","arxiv_id":"2212.05935","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2023.109834","authors":["Rubèn Tito","Dimosthenis Karatzas","Ernest Valveny"],"year":2023,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Introduces a hierarchical architecture for question answering over multi-page documents and the MP-DocVQA setting. It jointly handles page selection and answer generation, providing page-level provenance but not necessarily cell- or bounding-box-level evidence."}
{"title":"Document Understanding Dataset and Evaluation (DUDE)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.08455","arxiv_id":"2305.08455","authors":["Jordy Van Landeghem","Rubén Tito","Łukasz Borchmann","Michał Pietruszka","Paweł Józiak","Rafał Powalski","Dawid Jurkiewicz","Mickaël Coustaty","Bertrand Ackaert","Ernest Valveny","Matthew Blaschko","Sien Moens","Tomasz Stanisławek"],"year":2023,"abstract":"Provides a document-understanding benchmark spanning varied domains and multi-page, visually rich documents. Its diversity makes it useful for testing models beyond narrowly templated forms, while its results do not establish workplace-email accuracy by themselves."}
{"title":"MMLongBench-Doc: Benchmarking Long-context Document Understanding with Visualizations","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.01523","arxiv_id":"2407.01523","authors":["Yubo Ma","Yuhang Zang","Liangyu Chen","Meiqi Chen","Yizhu Jiao","Xinze Li","Xinyuan Lu","Ziyu Liu","Yan Ma","Xiaoyi Dong","Pan Zhang","Liangming Pan","Yu-Gang Jiang","Jiaqi Wang","Yixin Cao","Aixin Sun"],"year":2024,"abstract":"Benchmarks long-document multimodal understanding over PDFs containing text, images, charts, tables, and layout information. Questions may require locating evidence across pages, making the benchmark useful for studying cross-page reasoning and source attribution."}
{"title":"LongDocURL: a Comprehensive Multimodal Long Document Benchmark Integrating Understanding, Reasoning, and Locating","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.18424","arxiv_id":"2412.18424","doi":"10.18653/v1/2025.acl-long.57","authors":["Chao Deng","Jiale Yuan","Pi Bu","Peijie Wang","Zhong-Zhi Li","Jian Xu","Xiao-Hui Li","Yuan Gao","Jun Song","Bo Zheng","Cheng-Lin Liu"],"year":2025,"venue":"ACL","abstract":"Evaluates long multimodal documents with tasks spanning understanding, reasoning, and locating. Its explicit locating component is especially relevant to systems that must return not only an answer but also where supporting evidence occurs."}
{"title":"Where is this coming from? Making groundedness count in the evaluation of Document VQA models","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.19120","arxiv_id":"2503.19120","authors":["Armineh Nourbakhsh","Siddharth Parekh","Pranav Shetty","Zhao Jin","Sameena Shah","Carolyn Rose"],"year":2025,"venue":"Findings of NAACL","abstract":"Argues that answer correctness alone is insufficient for document question answering and explicitly evaluates whether answers are grounded in source document evidence. The work is directly relevant to provenance requirements that demand traceable support rather than plausible answer strings."}
{"title":"BBox DocVQA: A Large Scale Bounding Box Grounded Dataset for Enhancing Reasoning in Document Visual Question Answer","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.15090","arxiv_id":"2511.15090","authors":["Wenhan Yu","Wang Chen","Guanqiang Qi","Weikang Li","Yang Li","Lei Sha","Deguo Xia","Jizhou Huang"],"year":2025,"abstract":"Provides document VQA data with explicit bounding-box grounding for supporting evidence. It covers evidence involving one or multiple regions and documents, making it directly relevant to region-level provenance rather than page-only retrieval."}
{"title":"M3Grounder: Mask-Based Multi-Span and Multi-Granular Grounding for Document QA","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2026/html/Venna_M3Grounder_Mask-Based_Multi-Span_and_Multi-Granular_Grounding_for_Document_QA_CVPR_2026_paper.html","authors":["Venkata Kesav Venna","Sai Madhusudan Gunda","Jyothi Swaroopa Jinka","Hrithik Sagar Rachakonda","Anirudh Srinivasan","Ravi Kiran Sarvadevabhatla"],"year":2026,"venue":"CVPR","abstract":"Grounds document-QA evidence using masks and supports multiple evidence spans at different granularities such as phrases, lines, and blocks. This directly addresses precise localization of source evidence rather than only producing an answer or relevant page."}
{"title":"Multi-Page Document Visual Question Answering using Self-Attention Scoring Mechanism","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.19024","arxiv_id":"2404.19024","doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-70552-6_13","authors":["Lei Kang","Rubèn Pérez Tito","Ernest Valveny","Dimosthenis Karatzas"],"year":2024,"venue":"ICDAR","abstract":"Studies multi-page document VQA with a mechanism for scoring and selecting relevant pages before answering. It is useful supporting evidence for cross-page reasoning, but its localization granularity is page-level rather than precise cell or region grounding."}
{"title":"TableBank: A Benchmark Dataset for Table Detection and Recognition","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.01949","arxiv_id":"1903.01949","authors":["Minghao Li","Lei Cui","Shaohan Huang","Furu Wei","Ming Zhou","Zhoujun Li"],"year":2019,"abstract":"Introduces a large dataset derived from Word and LaTeX documents for table detection and table-structure recognition. Its recognition component makes it relevant to reconstructing tabular organization, while detection-only results are supporting rather than sufficient evidence for table understanding."}
{"title":"Image-based table recognition: data, model, and evaluation","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.10683","arxiv_id":"1911.10683","authors":["Xu Zhong","Elaheh ShafieiBavani","Antonio Jimeno Yepes"],"year":2020,"abstract":"Introduces PubTabNet and an image-to-structured-table approach that reconstructs table contents and HTML structure from document images. It also introduces a structure-aware evaluation measure, providing stronger evidence for preserving cell organization than table detection alone."}
{"title":"Robust Table Detection and Structure Recognition from Heterogeneous Document Images","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0031320322004861","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2022.109006","authors":["Chixiang Ma","Weihong Lin","Lei Sun","Qiang Huo"],"year":2023,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Addresses both table detection and reconstruction of table structure across heterogeneous document images. The structure-recognition component is directly relevant to preserving rows, columns, and cell relationships from attachments."}
{"title":"Table Structure Recognition and Form Parsing by End-to-End Object Detection and Relation Parsing","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0031320322004265","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2022.108946","authors":["Xiao-Hui Li","Fei Yin","He-Sen Dai","Cheng-Lin Liu"],"year":2023,"venue":"Pattern Recognition","abstract":"Combines detection of document objects with relation parsing to reconstruct table and form structures. Modeling relations among elements is relevant to preserving cell associations and form organization rather than extracting isolated values."}
{"title":"Table Structure Recognition using Top-Down and Bottom-Up Cues","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.04565","arxiv_id":"2010.04565","authors":["Sachin Raja","Ajoy Mondal","C. V. Jawahar"],"year":2020,"abstract":"Combines global and local visual cues to recover table structure from document images. The task includes structural reconstruction beyond locating the table region."}
{"title":"Visual Understanding of Complex Table Structures from Document Images","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.07129","arxiv_id":"2111.07129","authors":["Sachin Raja","Ajoy Mondal","C. V. Jawahar"],"year":2022,"abstract":"Targets visually complex tables whose semantics depend on nontrivial row, column, and spanning-cell organization. It is relevant to preserving structural relations that are easily lost when tables are flattened into plain text."}
{"title":"Multi-Type-TD-TSR -- Extracting Tables from Document Images using a Multi-stage Pipeline for Table Detection and Table Structure Recognition: from OCR to Structured Table Representations","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.11021","arxiv_id":"2105.11021","authors":["Pascal Fischer","Alen Smajic","Alexander Mehler","Giuseppe Abrami"],"year":2021,"abstract":"Presents a pipeline that converts document images into structured table representations through table detection and table-structure recognition. Its explicit structured output is relevant to retaining row-column relationships after extraction."}
{"title":"TUTA: Tree-based Transformers for Generally Structured Table Pre-training","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.12537","arxiv_id":"2010.12537","authors":["Zhiruo Wang","Haoyu Dong","Ran Jia","Jia Li","Zhiyi Fu","Shi Han","Dongmei Zhang"],"year":2021,"venue":"KDD","abstract":"Represents generally structured tables with tree-based positional and structural information and pretrains a transformer over that hierarchy. It directly addresses hierarchical headers and semantic table structure rather than treating tables as flat sequences."}
{"title":"TURL: Table Understanding through Representation Learning","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.14806","arxiv_id":"2006.14806","authors":["Xiang Deng","Huan Sun","Alyssa Lees","You Wu","Cong Yu"],"year":2020,"venue":"Proceedings of the VLDB Endowment","abstract":"Learns contextual representations for relational tables and applies them to table-understanding tasks involving entities and semantic relationships. Because its input is already structured tables, it is transferable to downstream reasoning but does not solve extraction from document images."}
{"title":"TaBERT: Pretraining for Joint Understanding of Textual and Tabular Data","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.745/","doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.745","authors":["Pengcheng Yin","Graham Neubig","Wen-tau Yih","Sebastian Riedel"],"year":2020,"venue":"ACL","abstract":"Pretrains representations jointly over natural-language text and semi-structured tables. It is relevant to reasoning over tables once their structure is available, but is transfer evidence rather than evidence for recovering table structure from images or attachments."}
{"title":"TaPas: Weakly Supervised Table Parsing via Pre-training","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.398/","doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.398","authors":["Jonathan Herzig","Pawel Krzysztof Nowak","Thomas Müller","Francesco Piccinno","Julian Martin Eisenschlos"],"year":2020,"venue":"ACL","abstract":"Pretrains a model for answering questions over tables using cell selection and aggregation. It demonstrates cell-level reasoning over already normalized tables, so it is transferable to downstream evidence selection rather than direct document-table extraction."}
{"title":"SpreadsheetLLM: Encoding Spreadsheets for Large Language Models","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.09025","arxiv_id":"2407.09025","authors":["Yuzhang Tian","Jianbo Zhao","Haoyu Dong","Junyu Xiong","Shiyu Xia","Mengyu Zhou","Yun Lin","José Cambronero","Yeye He","Shi Han","Dongmei Zhang"],"year":2024,"abstract":"Develops structure-aware encodings that preserve spreadsheet values, locations, formatting, and hierarchical organization while making workbooks tractable for language models. It is relevant to semantic understanding of existing spreadsheet structure and cell-addressable evidence."}
{"title":"PlotQA: Reasoning over Scientific Plots","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.00997","arxiv_id":"1909.00997","authors":["Nitesh Methani","Pritha Ganguly","Mitesh M. Khapra","Pratyush Kumar"],"year":2019,"abstract":"Introduces question answering over scientific plots with questions requiring extraction and reasoning over chart values. Its chart reasoning mechanisms are transferable to workplace attachments, though synthetic aspects of the benchmark limit claims about real-world extraction robustness."}
{"title":"ChartQA: A Benchmark for Question Answering about Charts with Visual and Logical Reasoning","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.10244","arxiv_id":"2203.10244","authors":["Ahmed Masry","Do Xuan Long","Jia Qing Tan","Shafiq Joty","Enamul Hoque"],"year":2022,"abstract":"Introduces chart question answering that combines visual recognition with logical and arithmetic reasoning. It includes real-world charts and is relevant to understanding chart-bearing documents, though answer correctness does not itself imply precise region grounding."}
{"title":"DePlot: One-shot visual language reasoning by plot-to-table translation","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.10505","arxiv_id":"2212.10505","authors":["Fangyu Liu","Julian Martin Eisenschlos","Francesco Piccinno","Syrine Krichene","Chenxi Pang","Kenton Lee","Mandar Joshi","Wenhu Chen","Nigel Collier","Yasemin Altun"],"year":2023,"venue":"Findings of ACL","abstract":"Converts chart images into linearized tables that can be consumed by language models for downstream reasoning. It is relevant to preserving the data structure behind visual plots, but does not by itself provide fine-grained visual provenance for every extracted value."}
{"title":"RefChartQA: Grounding Visual Answer on Chart Images through Instruction Tuning","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.23131","arxiv_id":"2503.23131","authors":["Alexander Vogel","Omar Moured","Yufan Chen","Jiaming Zhang","Rainer Stiefelhagen"],"year":2025,"abstract":"Extends chart question answering toward explicit visual grounding of answers in chart images. This makes it directly relevant to requirements where answers must be tied back to the chart elements or regions that support them."}
{"title":"Phrase Grounding by Soft-Label Chain Conditional Random Field","url":"https://aclanthology.org/D19-1515/","doi":"10.18653/v1/D19-1515","authors":["Jiacheng Liu","Julia Hockenmaier"],"year":2019,"venue":"EMNLP-IJCNLP","abstract":"Studies phrase grounding by linking textual phrases to image regions while modeling dependencies among grounding decisions. The experiments are on natural-image grounding, so the method is transfer evidence for document-region grounding rather than direct evidence about documents."}
{"title":"Scene-Text Oriented Referring Expression Comprehension","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9939075/","abstract":"Studies referring-expression grounding in images where scene text is important for identifying the referenced region. The task is transferable to screenshots and document surfaces because successful grounding depends on jointly interpreting text and visual location."}
{"title":"ColPali: Efficient Document Retrieval with Vision Language Models","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.01449","arxiv_id":"2407.01449","authors":["Manuel Faysse","Hugues Sibille","Tony Wu","Bilel Omrani","Gautier Viaud","Céline Hudelot","Pierre Colombo"],"year":2025,"venue":"ICLR","abstract":"Represents document pages directly with a vision-language model and performs late-interaction retrieval over their visual contents. It preserves more page-level visual information than text-only indexing, but retrieval is supporting evidence and does not provide precise cell- or region-level grounding by itself."}
{"title":"PDFFigures 2.0: Mining Figures from Research Papers","url":"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/jcdl/ClarkD16","doi":"10.1145/2910896.2910904","authors":["Christopher Andreas Clark","Santosh Kumar Divvala"],"year":2016,"venue":"JCDL","abstract":"Extracts figures, tables, captions, and their locations from scholarly PDFs. Its explicit association of visual objects with captions and page regions is relevant to preserving object-level provenance during document ingestion."}
{"title":"Figure and caption extraction from biomedical documents","url":"https://academic.oup.com/bioinformatics/article/35/21/4381/5428177","year":2019,"venue":"Bioinformatics","abstract":"Studies extraction and association of figures and their captions from biomedical documents. The capability is relevant to retaining figure-caption relationships and source locations rather than reducing documents to plain text."}
{"title":"Beyond Captions: Linking Figures with Abstract Sentences in Biomedical Articles","url":"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0039618","doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0039618","year":2012,"venue":"PLOS ONE","abstract":"Links scientific figures with textual sentences that describe or discuss them beyond the immediate caption. The work is transferable to resolving references between attachment prose and embedded visual content."}
{"title":"Semantic Text Matching for Long-Form Documents","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3308558.3313707","doi":"10.1145/3308558.3313707","authors":["Jyun-Yu Jiang","Mingyang Zhang","Cheng Li","Michael Bendersky","Nadav Golbandi","Marc Najork"],"year":2019,"venue":"The World Wide Web Conference","abstract":"Studies semantic matching for long documents and includes email attachment suggestion as an application. It provides direct evidence that email context can be matched semantically to attachment content, but the method is text-oriented and does not establish multimodal region-level grounding."}
{"title":"Leveraging personal metadata for Desktop search: The Beagle++ system","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1570826809000754","abstract":"Uses personal and contextual metadata to improve desktop search, including relationships between email messages and documents associated with them. It is supporting evidence for retaining email-to-attachment context, rather than evidence for multimodal document understanding or precise source grounding."}
===END llm_candidates.jsonl===
